---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ConstructionNotice from '../components/ConstructionNotice.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About this public engineering notebook.">
  <article class="content-shell">
    <header class="article-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">About this notebook</p>
      <h1>The projects are evidence.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This site follows an evolving way of thinking about software architecture through
        language, evidence, implementation, and long-term design.
      </p>
    </header>
    <ConstructionNotice />
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this exists</h2>
      <p>
        Tonesu began as a constructed-language project. Working on words, categories, scope,
        composition, and corpora made assumptions visible that ordinary software vocabulary
        often leaves implicit. Over time, that changed how later projects were designed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Tokimu, Tosumu, Weaver, and Anvil explore those lessons in very different domains. This
        notebook connects their discoveries without replacing their own documentation.
      </p>
      <h2>What belongs here</h2>
      <p>
        Durable ideas explain the current understanding. Project dossiers provide evidence.
        Journal entries preserve discovery and revision. The Architecture Atlas connects the
        vocabulary used across all three.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
